# arvo

The downstream facade of the arvo numeric stack. Re-exports the
public surface from every upstream crate, hosts default impls for the
trait contracts so consumers get composed numeric behaviour for free,
defines ergonomic `Int<const N: u16, S>` and `Uint<const N: u16, S>`
generic aliases, and hosts `UFixed<I, F, S>` / `IFixed<I, F, S>` as
`repr(transparent)` newtypes over `Bits<{I+F}, S, Unsigned>` /
`Bits<{1+I+F}, S, Signed>`. Float wrappers (`FastFloat`,
`StrictFloat`) live here too. Storage primitives (`Bits`, strategy
markers, `Bool`, `USize`, `Cap`, `IBits` / `FBits` / `Width`) live
upstream in `arvo-storage`. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.
